==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Amber Egg: N110''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Farmboy Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Farmboy Cat can be used similarly to [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]], but with higher range in exchange for having Single Target instead of Area Attack. Because of this, Farmboy Cat will have a difficult time dealing with swarms of enemies such as [[Gabriel]] and [[Mr. Angel]], or enemies with lower range as they absorb Farmboy's attacks.

Fortunately, with an excellent uptime of over 350% and higher range of 350, Farmboy Cat has his own excellent niche against [[Angelic Beast Rajakong]]: Farmboy can keep Rajakong at bay as the beast tends to push hard with other enemies, while keeping himself alive thanks to his [[Wave Attack|wave]] immunity and high range. The main issue, however, is that Rajakong is the only Angel Behemoth in the game, and [[Ancient Egg: N106 (Rare Cat)|Mushroom Cat]] already can be obtained earlier for countering the very Behemoth in offensive usage. Aside from countering Rajakong, he will seek more usage in later stages of the game where less peons are spammed in favor of more big enemies spawning, becoming a better choice over a talented Sanzo Cat in certain cases thanks to the perks mentioned above, being able to slow [[Boraphim]], [[Winged Pigge]], [[St. Dober]] and [[Lutrinae Gokurakko]] easily provided there aren't peons getting in the way of attacks. Speaking of Winged Pigge, this also opens up an entirely new strategy where you setup Winged Pigge to be slowed by Farmboy Cat and bombard it with heavy burst damage from units like Mushroom and [[Food Stall Cat (Rare Cat)|Cafeteria Cat]] WITHOUT using meatshields, as Winged Pigge stands at a low range of 170 and her Omni-Strike hits up to 340 range making it easier for units less than 340 range to kill her, and if you want the best insurance, [[Master of Mind Soractes (Special Cat)|Master of Mind Catcrates]] will shut down Winged Pigge completely with his freeze, making such a formidable Angel threat almost nothing but a nuisance at worst, solidifying its better usage over Sanzo Cat at this point.

You should still acknowledge its evolution price since it spends very valuable [[Catfruit|Blue Behemoth Gems]], though generally by the time you obtain the Egg for this unit, you would be able to grind for the Red and Purple stones easily.

